# generated by the mh-analog-designer tool's run_sim.py -- materialized from sch/cmos_vref/*.sch templates,
# regenerated on every run, not source
sch/cmos_vref.sch

# copied from the PDK's default xschemrc by the mh-analog-designer tool's run_sim.py; idempotently
# regenerated if missing
xschemrc

# simulation outputs: netlists, raw ngspice data, plots, per-variation run log.
# regenerable from the mh-analog-designer tool's run_sim.py + config.json; can grow very large across
# parameter sweeps. sim/variations.jsonl and sim/results.jsonl (directly under
# sim/, not matched by this pattern) are the compact logs worth tracking.
sim/*/

# trained surrogate models (weights + config + registry): tool-generated
# data from the mh-analog-designer "pro" distribution, never part of this
# project's own source -- and deliberately never tracked here at all, even
# the small config/registry files, since this repo is public and the
# surrogate-model feature is not.
models/

# stale leftover from a previous (sky130) revision of this project
simulations/

# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
